sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User<br/>(Wallet + own SSI agent)
    participant A as App<br/>(client + own SSI agent)
    participant C as CSS Server<br/>VcDidCommHttpHandler /<br/>AgentInitializer / AcpReader /<br/>PermissionBasedAuthorizer
    participant T as TTP<br/>(Trusted Third Party<br/>+ own SSI agent)

    rect rgb(230, 240, 255)
    note over U,A: DIDComm Exchange
    U->>A: DIDComm Exchange
    note over U: App authorized (for the User)
    note over A: User authorized (for the App)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 250, 230)
    note over U,C: HTTPS
    A->>C: HTTP GET resource(DID_a, DID_i, DID_u)
    C-->>A: 401 Unauthorized<br/>WWW-Authenticate: didcomm proofRequests=...
    note right of C: createDidCommAuthenticateHeader()<br/>(nonce + presentationExchange proof request)

    note over U,A: DIDComm — App collects the presentation from the User's wallet
    A->>U: Forward proof request<br/>(App ↔ Wallet exchange)
    U-->>A: Verifiable Presentation<br/>(agent / issuer / client DIDs,<br/>proof over challenge)

    A->>C: [HTTP] GET resource<br/>(header: vp = ...)
    C->>C: validNonceAndDomain(vp)
    C->>C: VpChecker.verifyNew(vp) →<br/>Credentials[agent, issuer, client]
    note over A: App authorized (for the Verifier)
    note over U: User authorized (for the Verifier)
    C->>C: AcpReader: matcher on agent/issuer/client<br/>→ acl:Read and/or acl:NRRead<br/>PermissionBasedAuthorizer: mode granted

    alt Read — 3a. Only acl:Read granted → serve directly
        C-->>A: 200 OK + resource
    end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 240, 240)
    note over U,T: NonRepudiationRead — 3b. Only acl:NRRead granted → CSS encrypts for the TTP escrow and attaches NRO
    note over C,T: DIDComm (only once - key rotation)
    C->>T: DIDComm Exchange
    C->>C: Fetch resource content,<br/>encrypt it with fresh sym key ⇒<br/>{ encryptedMessage }<br/>encrypt sym key with TTP-CSS<br/>shared secret ⇒<br/>{encryptedSymKey}
    C-->>A: [HTTP] encryptedMessage,<br/>encryptedSymKey,<br/>hash(resource, keyForDecrypt)<br/>NRO
    note right of C: attachNonRepudiationMaterial():<br/>NRO = signatureFromCSS on<br/>hash(resource, keyForDecrypt)

    note over U,C: 4. App signs the receipt (NRR) — then picks ONE of the two release paths below
    A->>A: Create and sign NRR: hash(resource, keyForDecrypt) (NRR)

    alt 5a. Release via CSS (App stays with the server it already talked to)
        A->>C: [HTTP] NRR
        C->>C: verifySignedResource(NRR) → match hash /<br/>requesterDid / requestedResource<br/>against the pending context
        C-->>A: [HTTP] keyForDecrypt
        note right of C: jwsGraphService.storeVerifiedJws(...)<br/>(CSS-side non-repudiation evidence)
    else 5b. Release via TTP (App goes straight to the escrow — alternative path)
        A->>T: [HTTP] checkResource(encryptedResource [with NRO], NRR,<br/>requestedResource, requesterDid)
        T->>T: Verify NRR Signature + NRO Consistency<br/>(hashCredential / signatureFromCSS),<br/>then ask the TTP to decrypt the encryptedSymKey
        T-->>A: [HTTP] keyForDecrypt
    end

    note over U,A: 6. Deliver resource to the user
    A->>A: Decrypt encryptedMessage locally<br/>with keyForDecrypt → plaintext resource
    A-->>U: Deliver resource to the User<br/>(app-specific)
    end
